```python
def abbrev_num(x):
    if x == 0:
        return "0"
    if abs(x) < 1000:
        return str(x)
    exp = int(math.floor(math.log10(abs(x))))
    suffix = "K" if exp < 6 else "M" if exp < 9 else "B" if exp < 12 else "T"
    digits = abs(x) / (10 ** (exp - 2))
    return f"{round(digits)}{suffix}"
``` [end of text]


